 "restricted_cohort_cluster_ci": {
  "method": "subject_id-clustered nonparametric bootstrap, 95% percentile interval. Unit of resampling = subject (patient); every admission of a drawn subject enters with the subject's draw count, so admissions of one patient are never treated as independent. Per seed: subjects of that seed's TEST set are drawn with replacement (as many as there are test subjects) and violation rate (violations / deployed severe decisions), coverage (deployed / severe) and ICD agreement (coded / severe) are recomputed on the surviving-strata severe cases; the median across seeds of (lo, hi) is reported. Pooled: all seeds' test decisions are stacked and subjects drawn from the union of test subjects; a subject appears in several seeds' test sets, so the pooled interval is DESCRIPTIVE of the stacked decisions, not an inferential interval for one draw.",
